 An AQL statement must at least contain the `SELECT` and `FROM` clauses.
 
+A query that follows the grammar is still invalid, and is rejected, when it:
+
+* names a class the RM does not define, or a path no RM class defines;
+* has a node predicate on a node that has no `_archetype_node_id_`, or an archetype predicate outside the `FROM` clause;
+* gives two column expressions the same name alias;
+* sorts by data that is not comparable, such as a whole object or a collection;
+* compares values of incompatible types, such as a `String` and an `Integer`.
+
